what should entrepreneurs study in  university so I got a great question for  my YouTube viewers love you guys Tassimo  who wouldn't say hi I'm going to watch  your videos on a daily basis as a matter  of fact I have two of your videos as my  morning routine Thank You Tassimo thanks  a lot for your work is life-changing I  would like to ask your help I'm applying  for college these days but I'm really  suffering aside what the study in  college as an entrepreneur I don't want  to end up as a professional after  graduation in other words what do you  think entrepreneurs ought of studying  universities that would be helpful on  the entrepreneurial process Thanks  Tassimo this is a fantastic question and  one that I feel personally connected to  because I had my first real success out  of the business that I started when I  was in university so I usually give  three steps but today I'm giving you  five steps on what to do and I hope that  it helps you on your journey  number one is small business classes you  want to take whatever small business  classes they have at your university and  there may be a whole program around it  or may just be one class I remember at  my university  I'm Communiversity of Toronto which is  one of the probably the most well-known  university in Canada and and pretty well  known around the world and they had one  class in entrepreneurship that's all  they had so I took that and and it was  honestly a little too simple I had  already started my business and I was  learning way more from from doing and  being in my business in that class but  but it's still helpful to have the  basics right if you have no background  you've never done anything around  entrepreneurship before it's helpful to  have some of the basics and whatever  classes they have there can help teach  you the side benefit of it is you're  also in a group right the people who are  in that class with of others who want to  be entrepreneurs too or have Inklings  and become entrepreneurs and so you may  make some great contacts great  connections great business partners by  going to the classes that are around  entrepreneurship and my first business  was out of university I was 19 years old  and it was with two  other students who are at the same  university as I was and that's how we  created the company that eventually I  built up and sold so take whatever  classes they have around  entrepreneurship number two classes  you're passionate about like anything  else if you want to have success you  have to be passionate about if you want  to be a successful entrepreneur then you  need to be passionate about what you're  doing and so use your opportunity and  university to learn about other subjects  that have nothing to do with business  but that you're excited about because  you'll find some way to infuse business  into it and that could be your first  mega success one of my favorite examples  here is Steve Jobs who the founder of  Apple and he dropped out of university  so he could drop in on classes that  dealt with typography and who's learning  about fonts and how to how to create  characters that look beautiful because  he was frustrated with the current fonts  on computer systems and when Apple first  came out with his first computers they  had beautiful typography and fonts built  in and that was one of the  differentiators one of the reasons that  people went to go use a Mac and so he  took this knowledge you know what does  sitting on a typography class and people  would look at that from the outside and  say what are you doing typography class  what does have to do with  entrepreneurship or starting your own  business and he may not have even known  at the time either but he found a way to  incorporate that passion of his into his  business to help make him successful so  look at the roster of classes that are  available and see what speaks to you  it's okay if it has nothing to do with  business maybe you're taking a history  class or computer class or or sports or  whatever it is you're taking something  that you feel passionate you have an  interest in because believe me that will  come back to pay really strong dividends  for you you will find a way to  incorporate that into your future  business number three entrepreneur  groups most universities in college have  an entrepreneur small business group it  may be a consulting group it may be  helping entrepreneurs get started and  giving them advice whatever it is you  want to join  and it does a couple things one it'll  start giving you a little bit of  experience so if it's an entrepreneur or  consulting group you can start working  with entrepreneurs and I'll give you a  little bit of a taste for what it's like  real world experiences that are just out  of a textbook and it also again  introduces you to more of the hardcore  entrepreneurs because the people who are  running and involved in those groups are  more likely going to be the people who  don't want to get a job afterwards I  want to go and launch their own business  and they're using this as testing ground  and so knowing those people will be  really helpful because when you're out  there in the world doing your own  company and you're struggling it's great  to have a network of other entrepreneurs  to talk to connect with share ideas  share resources share connections to  help each other grow so look for  whatever entrepreneur group is available  and join it and get involved number four  start your own business start on the  side do something right now you don't  have to wait for when you graduate to  start something even if it's not the  business you end up with just start  something now because you're going to  learn so much more from doing from the  practical knowledge of running a  business then you're going to learn from  a textbook or learning from a teacher  who isn't really an entrepreneur right  then we have guest lecturers come in who  are entrepreneurs and give advice but  your best learning is going to be from  doing so start something small now on  the side part time to start building up  your knowledge base and number five is  create your own class this isn't really  well known but in a lot of universities  and colleges you can create your own  class you can create your own credit by  working with one of the professors and  so what I did was I had my business and  I wanted to work with a professor to  create my own class and I went to  somebody in the marketing department and  we created a class about pricing and  basically what they do is they mentor  you you meet as often as you want to  meet as you set up with your professor  and at the end you have to create a  paper that you submit to them and they  grade it and give you a final mark so  you have no final exam the coursework is  a lot lighter because there is no  coursework it's whatever you decide as  long as you get the backing from  the professor's so I created this course  on pricing and I used it to support the  business that I had right look at look  back the step four start on the side I  had a business that was selling  scientific software and some of our  customers could be university labs and  so I was able to go in to the labs at my  University and ask some questions about  pricing and learn about what they were  doing learned about their their lab and  their setup and actually make a few  sales but I would never be allowed to go  in and sell but I could go in under a  university sponsored project to collect  data and research because that's what I  was doing from our coursework so it  teaches you how to run your own project  it gives you a little bit more project  management skills it allows you to pick  a topic that you're passionate about  that you want to learn about at that  time I wanted to really learn about  pricing and it may help the business  that you've started as well by giving  you some contacts and potentially some  of your own new customers so find the  professor who you can connect with and  create your own class with them  so to summarize the five steps take  small business classes take classes that  you're passionate about join  entrepreneur groups start your own  business and create your own class  believe for those are watching like the  video you can support me please by  clicking on the link in the description  below leave a comment let me know what  you think and click on my face to  subscribe to the channel thank you so  much I'll see you soon
 

